pcr-reset-handle-type: TPM2_PCR_Reset rejects TPM_RH_NULL with TPM_RC_VALUE

Classification: spec-deviation bug fix.

The pcrHandle of TPM2_PCR_Reset is a TPMI_DH_PCR without '+' (Part 3,
TPM2_PCR_Reset), so TPM_RH_NULL must be rejected while unmarshaling the
handle (TPM_RC_VALUE + TPM_RC_H + TPM_RC_1). Version 185 unmarshals it as
TPMI_DH_PCR+ and thus accepts TPM_RH_NULL (and fails later, e.g. with
TPM_RC_AUTH_MISSING).
diff --git a/TPMCmd/tpm/include/private/CommandDispatch.inl b/TPMCmd/tpm/include/private/CommandDispatch.inl
--- a/TPMCmd/tpm/include/private/CommandDispatch.inl
+++ b/TPMCmd/tpm/include/private/CommandDispatch.inl
@@ -640,7 +640,10 @@ MAKE_DISPATCH_TABLE(
 #define CURRENT_TPM_COMMAND PCR_Reset
 MAKE_DISPATCH_TABLE(
     // Command input handles
-    MAKE_INPUT_DISPATCH_ENTRY(MARSHAL_ID_TPMI_DH_PCR_Plus, pcrHandle),
+    // tpm-rs differential testing -- C-ref spec deviation fix (NOT determinism):
+    // pcrHandle is a TPMI_DH_PCR without '+' (Part 3, TPM2_PCR_Reset), so
+    // TPM_RH_NULL is TPM_RC_VALUE.
+    MAKE_INPUT_DISPATCH_ENTRY(MARSHAL_ID_TPMI_DH_PCR, pcrHandle),
 
     MAKE_DISPATCH_SEPARATOR(START_INPUT_PARAMETERS),
     // Command input parameters
